$ mp calendar --help
The calendar: list, view, show and hide calendars, free/busy, reminders, rebuild

Usage: mp calendar [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list       List the calendars: account, name, id, backend, visibility, colour
  view       Show the events of an agenda, a day or a week
  freebusy   Show when people and rooms are busy: the server's free/busy, your own first
  show       Make a calendar's events visible in the views again
  hide       Hide a calendar's events from the views (a local preference)
  reminders  List the reminders that fired and wait for you: summary, when, where, account and event id
  reminder   Dismiss or snooze one event's reminder, in every client and in Outlook
  rebuild    Report what the stored attendee REPLY emails resolve on the stored invitations, and resync the server calendar of an account that has one. The fold writes nothing: attendee statuses are derived from the `invite.ics` payloads wherever they are displayed, so there is no cached copy to rebuild. Covers every configured account unless `-A` names one
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
