$ mp calendar view --help
Show the events of an agenda, a day or a week

Usage: mp calendar view [OPTIONS] [LAYOUT]

Arguments:
  [LAYOUT]
          The layout

          Possible values:
          - agenda: Day by day, the days with events
          - day:    One day
          - week:   The ISO week, Monday to Sunday
          
          [default: agenda]

Options:
      --on <DATE>
          The day shown, or the first day of the agenda (default today)

      --from <DATE>
          The agenda's first day

      --to <DATE>
          The agenda's last day, included

  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>
          Only these accounts (repeatable; default every account)

      --calendar <ID>
          Only these calendar ids, as `mp calendar list` prints them (repeatable)

      --hidden
          Include the hidden calendars' events

      --zone <ZONE>
          The IANA zone to read the times in (default the local zone)

      --json
          Print the `calendar.view` answer as JSON on stdout

      --profile <NAME>
          Profile to run on, with its own config, data and daemon (default: $MAILYPOPPINS_PROFILE, else the default profile)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Dates: YYYY-MM-DD, today, tomorrow, yesterday, or +N / -N for N days from
today. The agenda runs from --on (default today) through 14 days later, or
from --from through --to; a day is --on; a week is the ISO week holding --on.
Each event line carries your answer: ✓ accepted, ~ tentative, ✗ declined,
? not answered, ★ organizer.

Examples:
  mp calendar view
  mp calendar view week --on +7
  mp calendar view day --on tomorrow -A evoqs
  mp calendar view --from 2026-08-01 --to 2026-08-31 --json

$ mp calendar freebusy --help
Show when people and rooms are busy: the server's free/busy, your own first

Usage: mp calendar freebusy [OPTIONS] [ADDRESS]...

Arguments:
  [ADDRESS]...  The people and room mailboxes to ask about (your own is always asked)

Options:
      --on <DATE>          The day (default today)
      --from <DATE>        The range's first day
      --to <DATE>          The range's last day, included
      --interval <MIN>     Minutes per slot, 5 to 1440 [default: 30]
      --zone <ZONE>        The IANA zone the days run in (default the local zone)
      --json               Print the settled `calendar.freebusy` result as JSON on stdout
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
      --profile <NAME>     Profile to run on, with its own config, data and daemon (default: $MAILYPOPPINS_PROFILE, else the default profile)
  -h, --help               Print help

Dates: YYYY-MM-DD, today, tomorrow, yesterday, or +N / -N for N days from
today; --on (default today) is one day, --from through --to a range of up to
61 days. Each glyph is one slot of --interval minutes: · free, ▒ tentative,
█ busy, ▓ away, ░ working elsewhere, ? unknown. An address outside your
organisation reads "no free/busy". Needs a Microsoft 365 account.

Examples:
  mp calendar freebusy -A evoqs ada@example.com room-1@example.com
  mp calendar freebusy -A evoqs --on tomorrow --interval 15 ada@example.com
  mp calendar freebusy -A evoqs --from +1 --to +5 ada@example.com --json

